      "text": [
        " دِيَةُ الْكَلْبِ السَّلُوقِيِّ أَرْبَعُونَ دِرْهَماً جَعَلَ ذَلِكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) وَ دِيَةُ كَلْبِ الْغَنَمِ كَبْشٌ وَ دِيَةُ كَلْبِ الزَّرْعِ جَرِيبٌ مِنْ بُرٍّ وَ دِيَةُ كَلْبِ الْأَهْلِيِّ قَفِيزٌ مِنْ تُرَابٍ لِأَهْلِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali, from his father, from Muhammad Bin Hafs, from Ali Bin Abu Hamza, from Abu Baseer, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from one of the two (5<sup>th</sup> or 6<sup>th</sup> Imam<sup>asws</sup>) having said: ‘Wergild of the greyhound dog is forty Dirhams, Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> made it to be that, and wergild of the shepherd dog, and the wergild of the plantation guard dog being a ‘<span class=\"iTxt\">Jareyb</span>’ (unit of measurement) from the wheat; and wergild of domesticated dog being a ‘<span class=\"iTxt\">Qafeez</span>’ (Unit of measurement) from the soil of its owners’."
        ]
      }
    },
